<section class="section" id="warm-up-pregame" data-section>
<div class="section-head">
<div>
<h2>Warm-Up • Pregame appetizers</h2>
<p>Start with the little things people keep reaching for. • 5 recipes</p>
</div>
<a class="top-link" href="#top">↑ Rounds</a>
</div>
<div class="recipe-list">
<details class="recipe" id="recipe-0" data-search="brandy old-fashioned glazed meatballs warm-up / pregame 1 lb 80/20 ground beef 1/3 cup plain breadcrumbs 1 large egg 2 tbsp finely grated or minced onion 1 tbsp worcestershire sauce 1 tsp kosher salt 1/2 tsp black pepper 1/2 tsp garlic powder 1 tbsp neutral oil, if baking 2 tbsp butter 1/3 cup brandy 1/3 cup packed brown sugar 1/4 cup beef broth 1 1/2 tbsp worcestershire sauce 1 tbsp orange marmalade or 2 tsp orange juice concentrate (optional but very old-fashioned-ish) 4 dashes aromatic bitters 1 tsp dijon mustard pinch of black pepper">
<summary>
<div>
<div class="r-title">Brandy Old-Fashioned Glazed Meatballs</div>
<div class="r-mini">
<span class="pill">⏱ 45 minutes</span>
<span class="pill">Easy–Moderate</span>
</div>
</div>
<span class="open-label">Open recipe</span>
</summary>
<div class="recipe-body">
<div class="meta-grid">
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Serves</span>3 people • about 15 small meatballs</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Total time</span>45 minutes</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Difficulty</span>Easy–Moderate</div>
<div class="meta-card">
<span>Equipment</span>Sheet pan or smoker-safe pan; medium skillet/saucepan; instant-read thermometer helpful.</div>
</div>
<div class="makeahead">
<b>Make-ahead:</b> Shape and bake/smoke the meatballs up to 1 day ahead. Rewarm them directly in the glaze.</div>
<div class="cols">
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Ingredients</h3>
<ul>
<li>1 lb 80/20 ground beef</li>
<li>1/3 cup plain breadcrumbs</li>
<li>1 large egg</li>
<li>2 tbsp finely grated or minced onion</li>
<li>1 tbsp Worcestershire sauce</li>
<li>1 tsp kosher salt</li>
<li>1/2 tsp black pepper</li>
<li>1/2 tsp garlic powder</li>
<li>1 tbsp neutral oil, if baking</li>
<li>2 tbsp butter</li>
<li>1/3 cup brandy</li>
<li>1/3 cup packed brown sugar</li>
<li>1/4 cup beef broth</li>
<li>1 1/2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce</li>
<li>1 tbsp orange marmalade or 2 tsp orange juice concentrate (optional but very Old-Fashioned-ish)</li>
<li>4 dashes aromatic bitters</li>
<li>1 tsp Dijon mustard</li>
<li>Pinch of black pepper</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="sub">Step-by-step</h3>
<ol>
<li>Heat the oven to 425°F, or set the smoker to 250°F. Line a sheet pan if baking.</li>
<li>In a bowl, combine beef, breadcrumbs, egg, onion, Worcestershire, salt, pepper and garlic powder. Mix just until evenly combined; overmixing makes meatballs dense.</li>
<li>Roll into 15 small meatballs, roughly 1 heaping tablespoon each. For the oven, lightly oil the pan and bake 12–15 minutes. For the smoker, smoke 35–45 minutes. Either way, cook until the centers reach 160°F.</li>
<li>While they cook, melt butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add brandy carefully and let it bubble 1–2 minutes. Stir in brown sugar, broth, Worcestershire, marmalade, bitters, Dijon and pepper.</li>
<li>Simmer the glaze 6–8 minutes, stirring occasionally, until glossy and just thick enough to coat a spoon.</li>
<li>Add the cooked meatballs to the glaze. Toss gently and simmer 3–5 minutes so the glaze clings to every meatball.</li>
<li>Transfer to a small warm serving dish and spoon the extra glaze over the top. Serve with toothpicks.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note">
